    "critique_and_refinement": "The raw Google Stitch generation proved overly verbose and crowded, featuring excessive mock telemetry pills (cluster VRAM, multi-GPU tags, DiT tags) and extraneous action buttons. For the actual React frontend implementation, we streamline the layout into a clean, modern, and uncluttered interface: focused side-by-side image comparison canvas, essential ML metric visualizers (routing probabilities, continuous gating weights, error heatmaps), and a clear persistent sidebar with genuine backend health monitoring."
